The remediation does address the two prior identity defects in the visible paths: manual IDs now hash a structured object, and both processed-input and seen-key duplicates derive their result ID from the persisted literature record. The critical remaining review is whether the new transaction journal and validator actually make those guarantees durable under recovery and whether the tests reach the failure boundaries rather than only the happy path.
